# What must never reach a commit.
#
# Rust repositories are rarely only Rust: an agent runs a helper script, an
# editor writes a workspace file, a reviewer opens the tree on a different
# operating system. Every entry below is something a contributor can produce
# without meaning to, grouped so a reader can tell why each one is here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Rust output
# Build artifacts are reproducible from source and dwarf the source itself.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. Both the test harness and the
# examples commit theirs: an exact dependency set is what makes a supply-chain
# review, an MSRV check and a reproducible build mean anything.

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Local tools
# Pinned, checksum-verified binaries installed by `just setup`. They belong to
# a machine, not to history.
.tools/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Run evidence
# Produced by the local gate and by CI. Published as workflow artifacts, never
# committed, so a stale report can never be mistaken for a current one.
**/*.cdx.json
**/*.sarif
coverage.lcov
lcov.info
audit.json
clippy.json
secrets.json
licenses.txt
msrv.tsv
hardening.txt
scorecard.json
scorecard.md
scorecard.svg
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
reports/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Credentials
# Never committed, and listed explicitly so an accidental `git add -A` cannot
# sweep one in. Secret scanning is the backstop, not the first line.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.toml
.netrc
.npmrc
.cargo/credentials
.cargo/credentials.toml

# ------------------------------------------------------- Other runtimes
# This repository is Rust, Just and Bash. These directories still appear when a
# contributor or an agent runs an ad-hoc helper, and none of them should ever be
# committed here.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
vendor/
.bundle/

# ---------------------------------------------------------- Operating systems
# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
# WSL writes this alternate data stream beside any file copied from Windows.
*:Zone.Identifier
# Linux
.directory
.Trash-*
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- Editors
# Shared settings may be committed deliberately by un-ignoring a specific file;
# per-user state never is.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#
.session
Session.vim
.vim/
.helix/
.zed/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
.history/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Archives
# Release payloads are built by CI and attached to a run, not stored in Git.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
SHA256SUMS
